  "revision": 1,
  "revised": "2026-11-15",
  "source": "Disproel Manual PowerSave II (rev. 11072018)",
  "sources": [
    {
      "title": "Manual PowerSave II",
      "version": "rev. 11072018",
      "url": "https://disproel.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/02/Manual-Powersave-II.pdf",
      "note": "Modbus register table",
      "accessed": "2026-11-15",
      "sha256": "883310122820b98a1e5d0aabf1912f88c910912f21b6243b5768ade29f939525"
    }
  ],
  "notes": [
    "Modbus RTU on RS-485, 1200 to 38400 bps, slave ID 1 to 247, parity none, even or odd; the display example shows 38.4 K, ID 001, no parity, assumed here.",
    "Registers 40001 to 42001 as printed in the manual, counted from 1 (address base 1); every value is 32-bit, two registers. The manual does not state the word order; big-endian is assumed.",
    "The step power and voltage registers are named in Spanish in the manual; 'step 1' to 'step 12' are the compensation steps.",
    "Selection codes (SEL 1 to 10) follow the manual's selection table; the step structure code 3 is printed as 'Entr' and is not listed.",
    "Reset settings, reset alarm limits, factory settings (41001 to 41005) and save changes (42001) are write-only: write a value to run them, and save to keep changes.",
    "Written from the manufacturer's manual; not tested on a device."
  ],
  "protocol": "rtu",
  "unit_id": 1,
  "baudrate": 38400,
  "parity": "N",
  "databits": 8,
  "stopbits": 1,
